  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented customer ID normalization. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Summary of Customer ID Normalization\n\n**New function in customers.js**\n- Added `normalizeId(id)` export that:\n  - Trims leading and trailing whitespace\n  - Converts to uppercase\n  - Example: `' c-007 '` \u2192 `'C-007'`\n\n**Updated getCustomer function**\n- Now normalizes the provided ID before looking up the customer\n- Allows finding customers with mixed-case IDs and spaces\n- Example: `getCustomer('c-003')` finds customer 'C-003'\n\n**Updated createInvoice function**\n- Now normalizes customer ID before validation and storage\n- Stores the normalized ID in the created invoice\n- This ensures consistency across all invoices\n- Example: Input `' c-001 '` is stored as `'C-001'`\n\n**Test coverage**\n- 122 total tests, all passing\n- Added 12 new tests for normalization:\n  - `normalizeId` function tests (trim, uppercase, mixed operations)\n  - `getCustomer` tests with normalized IDs (lowercase, spaces, mixed)\n  - `createInvoice` tests with normalized IDs (stores normalized ID, finds customers with denormalized input)\n  - Both in `invoices.test.js` and `customers.test.js`\n\nThe implementation ensures that customer IDs from external systems are normalized consistently, preventing issues caused by case variations or whitespace that often occur when data reaches the system from different sources.",
